.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-NODE-EXPORTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-node-exporter
.Nd run whichever node_exporter this distribution ships, with kldload's collectors
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar node_exporter-flags ...
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
kldload's drop-in for
.Pa node_exporter.service
starts the exporter with the collectors its dashboards need: the textfile
directory, per-process metrics, interrupts, and the memory-reclaim
counters.
.Nm
is what that drop-in starts: it runs the first node_exporter it finds, in
.Pa /usr/local/bin ,
then the Debian and Fedora package paths, with the flags it was given,
replacing itself with it.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0.
.El
.Pp
Anything else is node_exporter's.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/systemd/system/node_exporter.service.d/textfile.conf
The drop-in, with the flags.
.It Pa /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/
What the textfile collector reads; see
.Xr arcstats-exporter 8 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The exporter's own; 1, on standard error, when no node_exporter is
installed, so that the unit fails rather than sitting active with nothing
running.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page; the service starts it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# systemctl restart node_exporter
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arcstats-exporter 8 ,
.Xr kfire-exporter 8 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub-exporter 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-09-20 the drop-in named
.Pa /usr/local/bin/node_exporter ,
which nothing installed.
On Fedora, where the package's
.Pa node_exporter.service
is another name for its own service, that broke the working exporter:
every start failed, and the machine had no host metrics while its Metrics
view looked fine.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
